research/audit/wave5-dispatch/audit-alpha-wave5-a8-round3.log:29:**The dispatch's item hashes were the wrong normalisation.** All six came from `judge.mts`'s hash (only the `judge:` sub-block stripped); the adjudication ledger is consumed by `step8-guard`, which compares against `item-hash.mjs` (whole `verification:` block stripped). Copying them in would have written rows the guard can never match. The derived claim was also false: `cex-cauchy-rationals-no-rational-limit` has **not** changed — its normalised hash is still `beede7a2a1…`, identical to all three prior `false_positive` rows. Same for four of the other five. The apparent movement was a judge stamp.
