items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:27:
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:28:## Definition
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:29:
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:30:Throughout, $m \in \mathbb{N}$ with $m \ge 1$, and $\mathbb{R}^{m}$ carries the
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:31:Euclidean norm $\lVert\cdot\rVert_2$ of [[def-euclidean-inner-product]] and
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:32:[[def-p-norms-on-rn]], whose induced metric is the published $d_2$
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:33:([[lem-p-norms-are-norms-and-induce-the-published-metrics]],
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:34:[[lem-metrics-on-rn]]). A function into $\mathbb{R}^{m}$ is called
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:35:**vector-valued**.
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:36:
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:37:### Continuity
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:38:
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:39:Let $(X, d_X)$ be a metric space ([[def-metric-space]]), let $A \subseteq X$
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:40:carry the restricted metric $d_A$ ([[def-isometry-and-metric-embedding]]), let
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:41:$f : A \to \mathbb{R}^{m}$ and let $a \in A$. Then $f$ is **continuous at $a$**
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:42:when
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:43:
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:44:$$(\forall \varepsilon > 0)\ (\exists \delta > 0)\ (\forall x \in A)\ \bigl[\ d_X(x,a) < \delta \ \Longrightarrow\ \lVert f(x) - f(a)\rVert_2 < \varepsilon\ \bigr],$$
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:45:
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:46:with $\varepsilon, \delta$ ranging over the positive reals, and **continuous on
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:47:$A$** when it is continuous at every point of $A$.
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:48:
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:49:**This is not a new notion, and that is the point of writing it down.** Since
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:50:$\lVert f(x)-f(a)\rVert_2 = d_2\bigl(f(x),f(a)\bigr)$ and $d_A$ is the
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:51:restriction of $d_X$, the displayed condition is **verbatim** the condition of
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:52:[[def-metric-continuity]] for the map of metric spaces
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:53:$f : (A,d_A) \to (\mathbb{R}^{m}, d_2)$. So every theorem about continuous maps
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:54:of metric spaces applies to vector-valued functions with no translation, and
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:55:this library has exactly one notion of continuity here. The same move was made
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:56:once before, between the $\mathbb{R}$-native and the metric notions, in
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:57:[[lem-real-and-metric-notions-agree]]; this item is that move one dimension up in
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:58:the codomain.
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:59:
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:60:The two cases used below are $X = \mathbb{R}$ with $d_{\mathbb{R}}(s,t) = |s-t|$
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:61:([[lem-real-line-is-a-metric-space]]) and $X = \mathbb{R}^{n}$ with $d_2$, for
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:62:$n \ge 1$.
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:63:
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:64:### Limits, for a real domain
items/def-vector-valued-functions-limits-and-continuity.md:65:
